# Optional. A Google OAuth 2.0 *Web application* client ID, used to create
# Gmail drafts straight from the browser. Public by design — an OAuth client ID
# is not a secret, and this app has no server-side secrets at all.
#
# Leave it unset and the app still works; each user can paste their own client
# ID under Settings instead, and it stays in their browser.
#
# To create one: Google Cloud Console -> APIs & Services
#   1. Enable the Gmail API.
#   2. Credentials -> Create credentials -> OAuth client ID -> Web application.
#   3. Add your site's origin (e.g. https://mailsheet.example.com, and
#      http://localhost:3000 for local dev) under "Authorised JavaScript origins".
#      No redirect URI is needed — the token never leaves the page.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
